  "rationale": "The spec requires throughput >= 32 Msps and sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.44us for 32 burst requests. pipelined_m dominates the current front with 10/14 designs and best area 1449, so it gets 60% of the budget. pipelined gets 40% to explore whether its higher Fmax (shorter combinational paths) helps meet the tight 0.44us batch latency constraint, even at higher area. Both families are constrained to data_width 14..16 (W>=14 needed for 2^-12 accuracy) and n_iter 12..16 (sufficient for accuracy with moderate guards). frac_guard and angle_guard ranges cover the full accuracy/area trade-off. The system constraint (32 results in 0.44us) is the binding constraint: for pipelined_m with m=2, latency is ceil(N/2)+2 cycles, and 32 results take 32 cycles (1/cycle throughput), so total time is 32/Fmax us <= 0.44us requires Fmax >= 72.7 MHz. For m=4, latency is ceil(N/4)+2, but throughput is still 1/cycle, so the same Fmax requirement applies. The key trade-off is area (more registers for smaller m) vs Fmax (shorter paths for smaller m)."
